  "business_basis": "Chris confirmed M01-CARD-01 through 06 / CHG-012 through 016; exact projections are technical derivations, not GATE-2 approval.",
  "interpretation": {
    "projection": "Expected keys describe semantic projections, not mandatory implementation wire names. Tests must compute each actual value from exercised runtime state or artifacts, never echo scenario/expected as actual. Missing policy entries project has_no_data=None.",
    "baseline": "Fresh actual bytes and structured Spec from protected gate1-v0.1 plus registered baseline read-context; no cumulative scenario mutations. Old approved observed.has_no_data/no_data_reason remain untouched; new automatic flag lives in separate policy/decision layer.",
    "nontest_authorization": "Only synthetic data and fabricated explicitly labelled non-test authorization documents for boundary testing; they exercise production validation semantics, not real clinical/business approvals. A test-only model cannot produce real approvals. Positive non-test cases must use a separately constructed synthetic non-test model/read declaration, not toggle a test-only model silently.",
    "synthetic_facts": "Deterministic standalone model fixture built from literal facts stated per scenario. These unit cases supplement, and do not replace, actual-byte baseline/CLI cases.",
    "standard_rules": "TEST-* rules are local explicit versioned synthetic declarations with source/hash references. Their pass/fail proves supported rule execution and workflow routing, never real CDISC compliance or selected project IG/CT. No automatic standards version selection.",
    "reject": "A locating rejection, no new effective approval/confirmed reason, and no partial mutation to persisted business state. Exception-code spelling is not fixed.",
    "xml_target": "Logical future mapping contract only. No XML generation or full XSD/P21 check is implied.",
    "history": "Old decision content and old check outcomes remain unchanged; current applicability is separate. Reuse creates a current authorization/decision linked to predecessor, with invalidated downstream checks still requiring rerun.",
    "rework_close": "An upstream return is not resolution. Only a newly supplied corrected input plus re-executed reconciliation can demonstrate the original fact discrepancy disappeared.",
    "input_variants": "Each listed variants/rules_variants item is a mandatory subcase; do not test only the first."
  },
